Hey all!

I haven't posted any YASDs here yet, but I wanted to post this one
because it was my best pacifist game to date, and thought y'all might
like to hear about it.

HanClinto the gnomish healer had a very lucky beginning of the game.
Izchak and the tool store didn't have magic lamps, but the general
store had a blessed one! Score one! I wasn't sure what to wish for,
since I had a leash but no magic whistle. Archons still scare me, so
after chatting with friends on #nethack, we decided that a blessed
greased -2 thoroughly rusty thoroughly corroded magicbane would be a
good choice, because of the curse-absorbtion and (most importantly) --
the 1-turn Elbereth. I sometimes regretted that wish, but all-in-all,
it turned out to be pretty good. I E-camp like a fiend when playing
pacifist, and having it fairly guaranteed accessible in 1 turn like
that was pretty nice. It paid off pretty nicely as the game went on.

I avoided the bottom of the mines because I didn't have good MR (didn't
want to wield Magicbane, because even in as bad of shape as it was,
local wizmode tests showed that it would still instakill monsters who
were less than 15 HP, even as a gnome with 9 str). So I proceeded to
Sokoban. I was blessed to find a couple of cream pies. I named them
HeadbangingInsurance (since I lost my last few pacifists to bumpkills
rather than actual deaths), stashed one in my sack, and wielded them
for the rest of the game. Sidenote: My last pacifist game was lost to
bump-killing a newt while wielding a fortune cookie. Musta' been pretty
stale.

Here's where I made my first big mistake. On the way to Soko, I came to
Delphi, and was super-happy about it. My naked AC at this point was -1
(from the racket -- I credit-cloned every shop in Minetown) and with my
SLA and leather cloak and everything, I was down to -9 AC. I was
looking forward to getting to Xlvl 3, and in my haste, requested a
major consultation without having enough gold out. Right before I hit
'y', I realized I didn't have enough gold, but I decided to proceed,
figuring it would just tell me I didn't have enough gold.

Not so.

She gave me a worthless mathematical proof and took what gold I had
out, and didn't give me any experience. I panicked, got more gold out
of my sack and tried again. Got some good advice about the uses of
Elbereth, but no experience. In desperation, I tried a minor
consultation, but that didn't give me enough experience to even get to
level 2. :(

That sucked. I was considering quitting the game in favor of
restarting, but I had already gotten a very early wish, and didn't want
to look a gift horse in the mouth. So I proceeded to Sokoban.

On the second level of Soko, found a wand, E-tested it, "You may wish
for an object." Score again! I've never found a /oWishing outside of
the castle, so that was pretty stinkin' cool for me. 2 blessed scrolls
of charging later, I had no idea what else to wish for, so I decided to
proceed through Sokoban and see what ending it was. It was BoH, so
after cleaning out the zoo and heading back down a few more levels in
the dungeon, I finally decided to stop playing so riskily and use up my
wand. I found a Nailbunny bones that unfortunately wasn't one of his
best games, though it did leave me with a nice "oESP. I decided to wear
the amulet (because ESP is so nice for pacifists to see monsters coming
up to avoid bumpkills), and wish for SDSM and CoMR. My wand was now at
(1:2), and I wasn't sure what to wish for. I wasn't hurting for
anything at the time, as I had a maxed-out horse and a maxed-out dog as
pets. I was seriously considering getting a magic whistle + archon +
speed boots, but I hadn't id'd !oGL or ?oGeno yet (to reverse-geno
wraiths), and wanted to save that for a possible wish.

I continued down, found a couple of thrones, but didn't have shock
resistance or enough HP to withstand 30 HP of shocking if it were an
electric chair, so I didn't sit on them. Found a few zoos, etc. I went
down past the Rogue level to dlvl 17 and pressed ctrl-l to go right
down a corridor. At the end of the corridor, I met a freezing sphere
face to face. It exploded before I had a chance to do anything else. I
was at full health (16/16) and -15 AC. It took me down to -7 HP.

YAAD, or YASD -- I'm not sure, but I'm interested in hearing others
thoughts on this game.

